    {
      "text": "You must have a Microsoft Teams account to configure a webhook."
    },
    {
      "text": "This guide provides information on configuring webhooks using Microsoft Teams for Digital Experience (ZDX) alerts. The following instructions provide a sample configuration that you can use based on the user’s requirements."
    },
    {
      "item": "In Microsoft Teams:",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Select the team in which you want to add a channel for webhook notifications.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Click More Actions (…) > Add channel.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          18
        ],
        [
          20,
          21
        ],
        [
          25,
          36
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Enter the name of the channel and save your changes.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "On the Posts tab, where you can see the conversation, go to Channel > Connectors > Incoming Webhook > Configure.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 4,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          12
        ],
        [
          60,
          67
        ],
        [
          70,
          80
        ],
        [
          83,
          99
        ],
        [
          102,
          111
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Enter the name of the webhook. Adding an image is optional. Click Create.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 5,
      "strong": [
        [
          66,
          72
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Copy the Zscaler Webhook Channel’s URL from the webhook configuration page.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 6
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Save.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 7,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Create a webhook in the Zscaler Admin Console.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 2
    },
    {
      "item": "From the navigation menu, go to Digital Experience > Settings & Configurations > Webhooks.",
